{{for|the legacy cluster jewel passive skill|Intensity (passive skill)}}
'''Intensity''' is a counter for several in-game mechanics. Intensity is gained by using the skill that grants it and decays while [[moving]].

{{il|Intensify Support}} improves area damage and decreases area of effect as you gain Intensity. {{il|Pinpoint Support}} improves projectile damage and decreases the number of fired projectiles as you gain Intensity. {{il|Crackling Lance}} scales beam width, branching angle and damage with Intensity.

==Mechanics==
Without other items and passive skills, the maximum stack of Intensity is 3. An Intensity stack is lost once every 0.5 seconds while moving.

{{il|Intensify Support}} and {{il|Pinpoint Support}} cannot support [[trigger]]ed skills, [[Vaal skill]]s, [[instant]] skills, [[channelling]] skills, skills with a [[reservation]] or which create [[minion]]s, or skills used by [[totem]]s, [[trap]]s, or [[mine]]s. Similarly, Crackling Lance will only gain Intensity when you "cast it", implying you do not gain Intensity if the skill is used by totems, traps or mines, or if it is triggered.

When a gem is added to or removed from an item which currently has a skill with Intensity stacks socketed, those Intensity stacks are removed. The skill also stops gaining Intensity from (for example) the {{c|mod|Spells which have gained Intensity Recently gain 1 Intensity every 0.5 seconds}} modifier on {{il|Apex Mode}} until intensity is gained again. This means there are no known ways to interact Intensity with totems, traps, mines or triggering.

